text:
maya: quick PSA - new starter hit 'fetch is not defined' when running our JS SDK in a Vercel Edge demo. sample app uses package root import and blows up.

evan: yep that's the ESM bundle assuming global fetch. Node-only fallback (undici) shouldn't be shipped into the edge bundle.

grace: suggestion: split exports -> edge ESM (no undici) and node CJS (requires undici). update package.json exports and CI to test both.

toni: small safe pattern for docs:
```js
async function safeFetch() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  const { fetch } = await import('undici');
  return fetch;
}
```
Call inside handler, not at module top level.

maya: also ship a tiny index.d.ts with minimal Request/Response shapes so TS users without lib.dom don't get errors.

ci-bot: added CI jobs: samples:node18, samples:node16-undici, samples:miniflare. created issues: #4301 dual-build, #4302 types-shim, #4303 samples-ci.
